From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:22:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] serial: qcom-geni: turn the engine clocks on again after a
 restore

Suspend keeps an open port's serial engine clocked (it only drops the OPP
and interconnect votes), so the hibernation image records the engine's
clocks as enabled. A hibernation image is restored after a power cycle,
which turned those clocks off. The kernel that loaded the image does not
use every engine: on the Yoga Slim 7x it never opens the Bluetooth UART,
so that engine's clocks stay off while the restored kernel still counts
them as on. The restore then reaches the engine registers with their
clocks stopped and hangs.

Release and retake the engine resources in the restore callback, so the
clock framework turns the hardware on again before the port is set up.

Found with the persistent restore checkpoints on the Yoga Slim 7x: with
synchronous device PM the restored kernel's last callback entry was
a98000.serial (uart14, Bluetooth), with no return.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
index 9a20f897d..6a3eff61f 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -2180,9 +2180,24 @@ static int qcom_geni_serial_resume(struct device *dev)
 static int qcom_geni_serial_restore(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct qcom_geni_serial_port *port = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	int ret;
 
 	port->setup = false;
 
+	/*
+	 * Suspend keeps an open port's engine clocked, so the restored kernel
+	 * still counts its clocks as enabled. The power cycle turned them off,
+	 * and the engine registers cannot be reached until the clocks run
+	 * again. Release and retake them so the clock framework enables the
+	 * hardware before the port is set up.
+	 */
+	if (!pm_runtime_status_suspended(dev)) {
+		geni_se_resources_off(&port->se);
+		ret = geni_se_resources_on(&port->se);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	return qcom_geni_serial_resume(dev);
 }
 
